TACO algorithm attribution
==========================

The H128 adaptive-scale, normalized-Hadamard, dual-scale E4M3 codec in
src/taco/codec.hip adapts the algorithm in COCCL_TACO revision
ca717e05b6dd6d21fff4d2617d209c95be63f3ef,
src/device/compress/taco/taco.cu.

Copyright (c) 2025, Institute of Computing Technology, Chinese Academy of Sciences.
Developers: Xingchen Liu, Haoran Kong, Zheng Wei, Liyang Zhao, Yufan Wang,
Jinwu Yang, Dingwen Tao (advisor), Guangming Tan (advisor).

The original BSD-3-Clause license and source snapshot are preserved in
third_party/taco/LICENSE.txt and third_party/taco/upstream/. The implementation
was rewritten for HIP/DCU on 2026-11-08: shared-memory collectives without a
warp32 assumption, software E4M3FN conversion, a ctypes ABI, and an independent
FP64 CPU reference. No NVIDIA CUDA binary or COCCL shared library is used.

Flux design reference
---------------------
ByteDance Flux commit 19831ca2d820e3e782ed1d15d8b52d0898b78b26 (Apache-2.0).
The BW1000 backend is a new HIP/PyTorch BLAS macroblock implementation.
It does not compile or execute the upstream CUDA/CUTLASS Flux library.
Reference files and their original license are retained in third_party/flux/.

Interleaved production mapping
------------------------------
Entwine, arXiv:2609.11562v1, section 3.1 equation (1).
All ranks use destination=slot%world, within=slot//world.
The present backend applies the mapping to BLAS macroblocks, not CUDA CTAs.
